+        // hosted session's own `writeBatchStream` carries W7 drain accounting and
+        // its `stdout` carries prior-generation attribution, and neither is
+        // something the library can perform on its behalf. The table below is
+        // what a host that serves nothing gets, which is the whole filesystem.
+        const handler = extend[envelope.op] ?? ops[envelope.op];
